s5-4-p5 : Block
s5-4-p5 = prose (cons "For \(L:\mathsf{Lang}\), interpreting a checked program is ordinary host computation. The fact that the host can form a term \(\llbracket p\rrbracket_L\) and a dependent property \(P(\llbracket p\rrbracket_L)\) follows by constructing and applying the represented interpreter; it requires no new proof judgment. Fidelity to a published source standard is a separate, explicit adequacy relation between that standard's derivations and the represented judgments. The relation can be established by translations in both directions with their side conditions and round-trip properties. This distinguishes *being able to express a language's definition* from claiming fidelity for an unspecified or partial definition." nil)
